# Privacy Policy for ROE: Salmon Run

**Effective Date:** September 15, 2026  
**Last Updated:** September 15, 2026

This Privacy Policy explains how ROE ("we," "us," or "our") collects, uses, discloses, and safeguards your information when you download, install, play, or interact with our mobile game application, **ROE: Salmon Run** (the "Application" or "Game").

Please read this Privacy Policy carefully. By installing, accessing, or playing ROE: Salmon Run, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this policy. If you do not agree with the terms of this Privacy Policy, please do not access or play the Application.

---

## 1. Information We Collect

We prioritize user privacy and strive to minimize data collection. The Application operates primarily on your local device with limited network interactions necessary for monetization and game operational features.

### A. Information Automatically Collected
When you access or play the Game, certain information may be automatically collected by us or third-party service providers (such as advertising networks):
* **Device Identifiers:** Mobile device advertising identifiers (such as Apple IDFA or Google Advertising ID / GAID), IP address, device model, operating system version, screen resolution, and language settings.
* **Usage and Performance Data:** Game performance metrics, crash logs, diagnostic data, session duration, frame rates, and gameplay statistics (e.g., high scores, game state transitions).
* **Location Data:** Coarse, non-precise location data derived from your IP address (used primarily for regional ad targeting and compliance).

### B. Local Storage & Local Data
* **Gameplay Progress & Local Persistence:** High scores, medal achievements (Bronze, Silver, Gold, Platinum), and player preference settings are stored locally on your device using `localStorage` or `IndexedDB`.
* **Session State:** Information regarding session revives and rewarded ad state is stored locally on your device during gameplay.

### C. Information We Do NOT Collect
* **Personal Identifiable Information (PII):** We do not collect your name, email address, physical address, phone number, or social media accounts.
* **Precise Geolocation:** We do not collect or track precise GPS location data.
* **Microphone or Camera Data:** The Game utilizes web audio synthesis via the Web Audio API (`AudioContext`) and programmatic canvas graphics. We do not access or record audio or video from your device.

---

## 2. How We Use Your Information

We use the information collected for the following operational, analytical, and commercial purposes:
* **Game Functionality:** To maintain local high scores, save gameplay state, and provide retro audio and rendering features.
* **Monetization & Advertising:** To serve non-intrusive top/bottom banner advertisements and rewarded video advertisements for in-game continuations/revives.
* **Analytics & Performance Monitoring:** To monitor game stability, analyze collision physics/frame rate performance across hardware models, and diagnose software bugs or crashes.
* **Legal Compliance:** To ensure compliance with applicable privacy regulations and platform policies (Apple App Store Guidelines and Google Play Developer Policies).

---

## 3. Third-Party Services & Advertising

The Application incorporates third-party Software Development Kits (SDKs) and advertising hooks for monetization and analytics. These third-party services may collect information directly from your device.

### Integrated Third-Party Providers
* **Google AdMob / AdSense / Generic Ad Hooks:** Used to deliver banner ads and rewarded video ads. Google may use advertising IDs and cookies or device technologies to serve contextual or personalized ads.
  * You can opt out of personalized advertising on your device via:
    * **iOS:** Settings > Privacy & Security > Tracking (Disable "Allow Apps to Request to Track").
    * **Android:** Settings > Privacy > Ads > Delete Advertising ID or Reset Advertising ID.

---

## 4. Children’s Privacy Policy (COPPA & GDPR Compliance)

**ROE: Salmon Run** is designed as a general audience retro arcade game. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under the age of 13 (or 16 in the European Union). 

* If you are a parent or guardian and believe your child has provided personal information to us or third-party networks through the Application, please contact us immediately.
* If we become aware that personal data from a child under the applicable legal age has been collected without verifiable parental consent, we will take immediate steps to remove such information and disable ad-tracking hooks for that session.

---

## 5. Data Retention & Security

* **Local Storage:** Gameplay scores, session states, and localized settings remain on your device until you clear the application data, clear local browser storage, or uninstall the Application.
* **Security Measures:** We implement standard technical safeguards to protect system integrity. However, no method of transmission over the internet or electronic storage is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute data security.

---

## 6. Your Rights & Choices (GDPR & CCPA/CPRA)

Depending on your jurisdiction (e.g., European Economic Area, United Kingdom, California), you may have the following rights regarding your data:
* **Right to Opt-Out of Targeted Advertising:** You can restrict advertising tracking via your mobile operating system settings.
* **Right to Access & Deletion:** Since we do not maintain central accounts or user profiles, clearing the Application data or uninstalling the Game removes all locally stored data.
* **Non-Discrimination:** Exercising your privacy rights will not restrict your access to playing the core Game mechanics.

---

## 7. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be effective immediately upon posting the updated Privacy Policy within the Application or on our store listings. You are advised to review this Privacy Policy periodically for any changes.

